# Ansible – Short Command Notes

Setup: Two Debian 13 machines.

- Controller: Machine where Ansible commands are executed.
- Managed Node: Machine Ansible controls.

### 1. Install Ansible (Controller)

```
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ansible -y
ansible --version
```

### 2. Generate SSH key (Controller)

```
ssh-keygen -t ed25519
```

Press Enter to accept the default file location.

### 3. Copy SSH key to Managed Node (Controller)

```
ssh-copy-id USER@MANAGED_NODE_IP
```

Test SSH:

```
ssh USER@MANAGED_NODE_IP
```

### 4. Create Inventory File (Controller)

```
sudo nano /etc/ansible/hosts
```

Add:

```
[webservers]
MANAGED_NODE_IP ansible_user=USER
```

### 5. Test Ansible Connectivity (Controller)

```
ansible all -m ping
```

Expected result: `"ping": "pong"`

### 6. Run a Command on Managed Node

```
ansible all -m command -a "hostname"
```

### 7. Create Apache Playbook (Controller)

```
nano apache.yml
```

Add:

```
---
- name: Install and start Apache
  hosts: webservers
  become: yes

  tasks:
    - name: Install Apache
      apt:
        name: apache2
        state: present
        update_cache: yes

    - name: Start Apache
      service:
        name: apache2
        state: started
        enabled: yes

    - name: Create web page
      copy:
        content: "Apache deployed using Ansible!"
        dest: /var/www/html/index.html
```

### 8. Execute Playbook (Controller)

```
ansible-playbook apache.yml
```

### 9. Verify Apache (Managed Node)

```
sudo systemctl status apache2
curl http://localhost
```

You can also open this in your browser:

```
http://MANAGED_NODE_IP
